WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.601
Officials with the NTSB are

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.469
on the ground

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.304
in Stanton, Virginia, investigating

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.439
what led to a private plane crash,

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.307
a plane

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:08.274
that just before

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:08.641
the crash

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.043
was intercepted by us

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:10.777
fighter jets

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.812
for violating restricted airspace

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.447
over Washington, D.C.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:17.784
The plane was a Cessna five 60 citation

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.552
similar to what you're looking at here.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.820
It took off from an airport

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.388
in Elizabeth,

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:22.022
ten, ten,

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:25.125
Tennessee at one 13 yesterday afternoon.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:26.793
It was bound for Long Island,

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.395
New York, you see there.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:29.496
But according to flight data,

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:30.397
the plane never landed

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.064
and instead

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.166
it turned around over Long Island.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.701
And then at 305 P.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.070
M, it flew over restricted airspace.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:37.771
U.S.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:38.538
Capitol Police

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:39.873
placed the capital complex

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.274
on an elevated alert

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.475
and officials tried

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.477
but were unable to make contact

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:45.678
with the pilot.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:46.279
That is one.

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.548
F-16s were scrambled to intercept

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.549
the plane

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.483
when they were author

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.052
and they were authorized to travel

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.053
at supersonic speeds

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.587
in order to get there in time,

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.189
which created the sonic boom

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.690
that was heard and felt

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.259
across the Washington area.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:08.835
According to

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.303
officials, those F-16s

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.939
reached the Cessna around 3:20 p.m..

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:13.640
And the Jets,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.241
they even set off flares in an effort

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.476
to get the pilot's attention.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.011
They never made contact.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.112
And the Cessna

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.046
eventually crashed

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.014
near the George Washington

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.749
National Forest in Virginia.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.484
CNN's Brian Todd is near

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.585
the site of the crash.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:26.719
He's joining us now.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:27.320
Brian,

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.021
where do things

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:31.391
stand with this investigation now?

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:33.226
Well, Kate,

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.594
we've got some new information for you

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:35.095
this morning.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:35.695
I just spoke

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.530
to a group of first responders

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.566
who were the first people on the scene

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.433
of that plane crash.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.301
And to give you a sense

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:42.735
of what they were up against.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.170
I'm going to take you to my right,

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:44.737
your left.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:45.638
We're going to pan into that

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:46.673
ravine up there.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:47.640
You can see how steep

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.275
the terrain is over over here.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.777
And you can see the patchy fog

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.712
that has settled in over

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:53.446
that little valley

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.781
area of that ravine area there.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.549
That is what they were up against.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.551
That fog was here last night

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.120
when the first responders got here.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.654
What they told us was

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.022
that they had to leave their vehicles

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.891
not too far from where I'm standing here,

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.292
just up the road a bit.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.827
And they left their vehicles

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.463
at just before 6:00 p.m. Eastern Time.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.699
If then took them 2 hours,

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:13.766
fully 2 hours

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.668
to walk into those mountains

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:16.870
in very steep terrain,

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.871
and they described it

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:18.371
as sometimes

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.072
being at an angle

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:19.806
like this

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.408
more severe than a 45 degree angle.

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:23.743
Getting to that site.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:24.844
It took them more than 2 hours.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.312
They arrived on the scene

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.147
of the plane crash.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.349
They started just after 8:00 p.m.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.517
Eastern Time.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.284
And what they found

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.519
was a very grisly scene.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.087
One of the first responders said

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:34.387
there were

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.421
maybe four

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.689
or five recognizable

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.324
pieces of wreckage there.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.759
But then he said beyond that,

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.494
nothing bigger than your arm.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.996
They did find human remains,

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:43.530
but again,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.532
nothing really recognizable there.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:47.767
And they believe that the plane

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:48.168
they said

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:48.902
that the plane left

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.370
a crater in the ground

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.538
They believe that

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:53.173
based on what they saw there,

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.007
that the plane went in

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.675
at a very steep angle

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.110
and that it took them several hours

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.444
to kind of process their way

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.279
through the scene

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.680
and then get back to their vehicles.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.348
They did not get back to their vehicles

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.918
until about 11, 15 p.m. last night.

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.452
So the the track to get in

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.421
there was dangerous and arduous.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:09.722
And when they got there,

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.623
they found really

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.225
just a lot of small, small

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:13.626
pieces of wreckage, Kate.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.962
And that investigation continues.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.797
NTSB back on site today.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.832
Brian Todd is there. Thank you, Brian.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.001
My team joins us now.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.204
How can something like this happen?

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:24.637
You know what's

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.471
so disturbing

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.105
here, Poppy,

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:29.108
is why the pilot on board this plane

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.177
and why the other people on board

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.879
this plane were unresponsive

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.180
to this military fighter

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.915
jet interception.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.951
Really alarming details here.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:38.818
And the big question

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.453
now is whether or not

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:41.454
this private jet,

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.989
a Cessna Citation, sits

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.391
between about seven and ten people.

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:47.827
The air inside is pressurized,

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:48.962
meaning that it makes it

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:51.097
breathable, more compressed,

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.933
not breathable outside at high altitude.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.536
If there was a rapid decompression

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.272
in this case, meaning that the air inside

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.273
woosh is out

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.741
because of some mechanical failure,

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.276
maybe the door was open

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.677
or there was a cracked window,

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.512
maybe something in the structural

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.047
integrity of the airplane

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:11.117
If you're up high at 34,000 feet,

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.853
the pilots have very little time

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:14.821
to respond.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.788
10,000 feet.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.323
They've got a lot of time to respond.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.625
25,000 feet,

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:19.726
three to 5 minutes

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:22.495
and put on an oxygen mask. 35,000 feet.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:25.231
30 to 60 seconds.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.366
That is one.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.401
Hypoxia starts to set in.

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:30.536
It's really the insidious killer.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.972
It's very hard for pilots to recognize.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.607
I can tell you, as a pilot

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:35.775
and flight instructor,

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:36.876
the first symptoms

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.511
your fingernails go blue,

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:39.545
then you start to get

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.214
a bit of visual impairment.

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:43.082
Also, maybe acting a little drunk,

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.517
maybe a little giddy.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.252
And then, of course,

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.720
judgment impairment

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.989
and you could slip into unconsciousness.

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:51.691
It's very, very dangerous.

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:53.893
And this is something that the NTSB

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.495
will have to look at here.

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:56.596
They really have their work

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:57.297
cut out for them.

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.831
Now, to try and figure out

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.867
if this is, in fact, the case.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:02.235
A lot of aviation

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.803
experts I'm talking to say

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.204
that is likely.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.173
Can't rule it out just yet

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.242
because this sounds on paper

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:10.977
at least very similar

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:14.247
to the Payne Stewart crash of 1999.

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:15.014
You may remember that

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.183
pro golfer was on board a Lear jet

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:19.118
at 40,000 feet.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.654
Fighter jets also set up to intercept

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:22.622
that plane.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:25.058
That plane crashed in an unpopulated area

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:26.326
in South Dakota.

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:27.427
In this case,

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:29.595
this plane crashed in unpopulated area

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:30.630
in Virginia.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.165
A lot of big questions here

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.200
that investigators will look into, Poppy.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.234
It's really scary

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.303
and just so sad for lives lost

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.338
Appreciate the reporting.

